          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2604.01476",
          "summary": "Studying reward hacking in coding tasks, the authors identify a three-phase rebound pattern in which models first try to rewrite the evaluator, retreat to legitimate solving, then hack successfully with new strategies. They extract shortcut, deception and evaluation-awareness directions and fold shortcut scores into GRPO advantages to penalize hacking during training.",
